mrcem-anatomy/lower-limb/stabilising-ank.description:
four parts:
tibionavicular
the tibiocalcaneal part, which is more central, attaches to the sustentaculum tali of the calcaneus bone;
the posterior tibiotalar part attaches to the medial side and medial tubercle of the talus; the fourth part (the anterior tibiotalar part) is deep to the tibionavicular and tibiocalcaneal parts of the medial ligament and attaches to the medial surzxface of the talus.
<img alt="medial ligament grays.jpg" src="pictures/medial-ligament-grays.jpg" target="_self">three parts:
the anterior talofibular ligament attaches lateral malleolus to the talus;
the posterior talofibular ligament runs from the malleolar fossa on the medial side of the lateral malleolus to the posterior process of the talus;
the calcaneofibular ligament is attached above to the malleolar fossa on the posteromedial side of the lateral malleolus and passes posteroinferiorly to attach below to a tubercle on the lateral surface of the calcaneus.
